# Cursor Rules for FastEndpoints Clean Architecture Template

You are an expert .NET, C#, and FastEndpoints senior engineer.

## Architecture Guidelines
- Follow Clean Architecture + Vertical Slice REPR pattern.
- Api layer uses FastEndpoints (`Endpoint<TRequest, TResponse>`). Never use MVC controllers.
- Domain is pure C# (no EF Core dependencies).
- Application has interfaces, DTOs, and application logic.
- Infrastructure implements persistence (EF Core, DbContext).
- Central Package Management (CPM) is enabled in `Directory.Packages.props`. Never specify `Version` in `.csproj` files.

## Coding Standards
- C# latest with file-scoped namespaces (`namespace Foo;`).
- Prefer primary constructors for classes with injected dependencies.
- Return responses using FastEndpoints fluent `Send` property: `await Send.OkAsync(...)`, `await Send.CreatedAtAsync(...)`, `await Send.NotFoundAsync(...)`.
- Validate requests with FluentValidation using `Validator<TRequest>`.

## Running & Testing
- Always verify changes with `dotnet test`.
- All tests (Unit, Architecture, Integration) must pass before completing work.
